OL,3,AOpenAI boss says world 'right to be
OL,4,Aafraid' but 'should trust' AI firms
OL,5,
OL,6,FOpenAI boss Sam Altman thinks people
OL,7,Fshould have more faith in his company
OL,8,Fand others like it to do the right
OL,9,Fthing when it comes to artificial
OL,10,Fintelligence (AI) development amid
OL,11,Frising public concerns about all the
OL,12,Frisks.
OL,14,F"The world should trust that we are
OL,15,Fgoing to do the right thing because
OL,16,Fit's the right thing and we feel the
OL,17,Fmagnitude of this," Altman said on
OL,18,FTuesday during a conference in San
OL,19,FFrancisco.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,107,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11904
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1789523291
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AOpenAI boss says world 'right to be
OL,4,Aafraid' but 'should trust' AI firms
OL,5,
OL,6,FHowever, Altman noted that people were
OL,7,Fjustified in their fears around AI, as
OL,8,Fthe capability of the tools has
OL,9,Fprogressed rapidly.
OL,11,F"It doesn't take as much imagination as
OL,12,Fit used to for [us] to imagine how this
OL,13,Fcould go wrong," he said. "I think the
OL,14,Fworld is right to be afraid of this."
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG4/19
